+++ b/canonical/03_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md
@@ -1629,6 +1629,8 @@
 
 **Single applicability read contract:** Model Studio authoring may display a newest draft, while CURRENT generation, dispatch, mapping/coverage projections, REST/MCP declarations and delayed jobs resolve the separately selected approved revision. Historical inspection is explicit and cannot silently become current execution. Update every material reader and writer together; incompatible old clients must receive a truthful unsupported/conflict response rather than fall back to latest. Retain declared-scope conflict and unsupported multi-scope rules in MBT-C-12. Source physical names are an implementation fit question, not permission to change accepted semantics.
 
+**Operation grain:** A single protected model dispatch/publication must commit its required native effect and provenance together. Retained MBT-AC-37 also permits separately authorized native creation, attachment and mapping stages to report truthful PARTIAL with durable committed receipts. Preserve that valid workflow; do not conflate independent actions into a fictitious all-provider transaction or use a partial-stage receipt to claim the single protected operation was atomic.
+
 **Migration admission:** Inventory legacy rows and affected interfaces; preserve native identity and immutable historical evidence; classify reconstructable versus unknown facts; define backfill only from authentic records; make a new present human decision where required; verify rollback and reader compatibility before enabling the new reliance path. Neither an agent's plausible reconstruction nor an existing `approved` flag proves a missing historic scope, actor class, selected revision or decision.
 
 **Evidence boundary:** Close these implementation gaps only with the implemented head, complete affected-owner/consumer inventory and allowed/denied/fault/retry/concurrency proof at the real native transaction boundary. Documentation now names the convergence work; the findings remain open as implementation prerequisites. Canonical 05 allocates the discriminating checks to existing MBT/ASE families without inflating scenario counts. Authentic UI baselines, actual authority policy, resource limits and the original QA round trip retain their separate gates.
